 36K  c  Compiled by J. Chen (NSCL, MSU), July 17, 2015.                        
 36K  c  2015Ro12: E=140 MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca beam was produced from the coupled 
 36K 2c  cyclotrons at NSCL. Fragments were separated by A1900 fragment         
 36K 3c  separator and transported to the beam cooling and laser spectroscopy   
 36K 4c  (BECOLA) facility. Measured hyperfine spectra using an optical pumping 
 36K 5c  and subsequent |b-decay asymmetry detection technique. Deduced charge  
 36K 6c  radii, isotope shift. Comparisons with shell-model calculations.       
